id: E2179-draft-2301_80739235
draft: true
title: "CMake C++ 日志库的 OHOS 可选后端闭包与跨编译测试边界"
category: cmake, conan, ohos, cross-build, dependency-closure, ctest
match_keywords: >
  CMake BUILD_SHARED_LIBS, LOG4CPLUS_QT4, LOG4CPLUS_QT5, WITH_ICONV,
  find_package Threads, OHOS cross CTest, Conan CMakeDeps target,
  cross_building test skip, target consumer smoke
root_cause: >
  CMake projects often expose optional GUI, encoding, or helper-server backends
  beside a small core library. Leaving those switches at upstream defaults can
  turn a simple OHOS library into an unpublished desktop dependency closure.
  A generic Conan OHOS profile can also omit the CMake system name, compiler
  target, and sysroot, causing the Windows linker to be selected. A cross build
  compiles CTest binaries that cannot run on the Windows host, so compile
  coverage and target runtime evidence must remain separate.
error_signature: >
  find_package\\(Qt|iconv.*not found|CMake Error.*Threads|Exec format error|
  cannot execute binary file|Missing binary.*optional backend
trigger_tool: cmake, conan, ctest, ohos-runner
phase: dependency-w0, configure, build, test_package, target-validation
severity: 2
rec_approach: >
  Freeze the upstream source and release hash, map each CMake option to the
  intended target closure, explicitly disable optional backends not required by
  the public API, and keep the platform Threads dependency as a system edge.
  Compile the upstream tests during cross build, run them only on a matching
  host or target, and use a Conan CMakeDeps consumer to prove the installed
  target name and logger API. Bind the Conan OHOS system name, target triple,
  and sysroot in both recipe and consumer; when the network is unavailable,
  allow a task-local source archive only through an explicit override while
  retaining the official URL and hash in recipe metadata.
rec_command: >
  cmake -S . -B build -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON
  -DLOG4CPLUS_BUILD_LOGGINGSERVER=OFF -DLOG4CPLUS_QT4=OFF
  -DLOG4CPLUS_QT5=OFF -DWITH_ICONV=OFF -DWITH_UNIT_TESTS=ON
verification_cmd: >
  require CMake configure/build success, an upstream CTest inventory bound to
  the same source hash, Conan consumer 1/1 on a runnable platform, and a target
  consumer smoke after native signing when the build is cross-compiled.
affected_scope: >
  CMake C++ libraries whose default build enables optional desktop backends or
  registers host-incompatible tests. The explicit option binding is reusable
  only when source inspection proves the disabled backend is not part of the
  required API or runtime closure.
safety_boundary: >
  Do not claim that disabling an option proves the backend is portable, and do
  not treat skipped cross CTest execution as PASS. Keep target execution,
  signing, binary closure, and postrelease evidence as separate gates.
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E2179-draft-2301_80739235.md
